<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-late-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Gasterosteus doryssus_late Turing wavelength at 27 µm (9.99 Ma) (Gasterosteus doryssus_late)",
        "Gasterosteus doryssus_late Turing wavelength at 27 µm (9.99 Ma) faithfully reproduces Gasterosteus doryssus_late morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-late-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-late-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-late-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-late-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Gasterosteus doryssus_late specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-late-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Gasterosteus doryssus_late" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not claim a second assessor or a kernel-checked Lean build",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim fossil melanophores were measured at 27 µm",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the gallery JPEG is a photograph of a Miocene specimen",
        "does_not_claim: Does not reuse the 1.7 mm parameters of slot 1209",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Du scaled with lambda_m squared across mid (33.62 µm), late (27.07 µm) and marine (21.48 µm)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Far-field spiral used as the late ocellus render, arm spacing measured on the native frame",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg parameters with r=25 so the continuum fastest mode is 27.07 µm",
        "reported_in_source: Hunt, Bell and Travis 2008 document pelvic evolution in a fossil stickleback lineage",
        "reported_in_source: Kondo and Miura 2010 treat pigment patterns as reaction-diffusion wavelengths",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation and diffusion-driven instability",
        "transfer_boundary: 27 µm is the tier-4 detail assignment, not a caliper reading on Truckee material",
        "transfer_boundary: The gallery plate is an illustrated ocellus card with a 100 µm bar" ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Gasterosteus doryssus_late (Late Miocene (Truckee Fm, 9.99 Ma))" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
